    regime: "Markets are closed, so every price in this file is Friday October 16 settlement re-verified on TradingEconomics this morning, and nothing in the tape has changed since the last report. What has changed is the reading of it. The single most informative fact on this board is a non-event: in a week that produced the highest Brent close since May at 109.860, a missile strike near Yanbu, Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries, an 8.6 million barrel US crude draw and an eight-session semiconductor slide that is the longest since 2008, gold fell 0.66% and silver fell 6.27%. An oil shock, a shooting war and a credit scare arrived together and the classic haven did not bid. That says the market is pricing this as a supply shock central banks must lean against rather than a risk-off event they will cut into - which is the frame for the whole board, and it is why the euro comes down to zero and the metals go short.",
